cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these waveforms, reports or tools, please cite this record and
  also state the limits listed in data/reports/dataset_limitations.md. The
  data are bench measurements against a BP Pump 2 simulator, not a clinical
  validation, and they do not establish conformity with ISO 81060-2.
title: >-
  Oscillometric cuff-pressure waveform dataset from a non-human bench
  (MPXV5050GP + ADS1115 + STM32F103ZET6)
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: linchuangrui
version: "2026-11-26"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: MIT AND CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lcr-123/blood-pressure-oscillometric-bench"
# No doi and no license-url on purpose: no DOI has been minted, and a
# license-url would point at GitHub's own licence detection rather than at the
# LICENSE.md that separates the data licence from the code licence. Add the DOI
# only after an archive that mints one exists.
keywords:
  - oscillometric blood pressure
  - cuff pressure waveform
  - non-human bench
  - dataset
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  645 synchronized cuff-pressure exports recorded on a bench against a
  Fluke BP Pump 2 simulator, together with the firmware, the acquisition
  protocol, the frozen estimators and the analysis reports that score them.
  The published corpus is 62 rounds; the remaining rounds exist as a
  development and evaluation set. Pressure was calibrated with two
  parameters per axis: 82.326 mmHg/V and -19.887 mmHg for every capture up to
  2026-11-26, and 81.529 mmHg/V with -20.03 mmHg afterwards.
preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: >-
    Oscillometric cuff-pressure waveform dataset from a non-human bench,
    with the frozen reference estimator and the cross-day batch verdict
  authors:
    - name: linchuangrui
  year: 2026
  notes: >-
    Repository record, not a journal article. Cite a commit hash together with
    the version above, because the reports and the frozen records are versioned
    in the same history. Use a hash that the remote actually serves: the
    published remote history is a single orphan snapshot, so the local
    development hashes quoted inside some reports (d022013, c60ef1f, 2430964,
    0bf20b5, 5066fc5, 7b0a04d, d7db003) are not resolvable there and are
    catalogued in data/reports/release_blockers_20261126.md section 7.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: Dataset limits and the minimum claim set
    authors:
      - name: linchuangrui
    year: 2026
    location:
      path: data/reports/dataset_limitations.md
  - type: generic
    title: What this dataset can and cannot support
    authors:
      - name: linchuangrui
    year: 2026
    location:
      path: data/reports/dataset_scope_statement.md
  - type: generic
    title: Pressure axis refit of 2026-11-26
    authors:
      - name: linchuangrui
    year: 2026
    location:
      path: data/reports/pressure_axis_refit_20261126.md
